    historical_tag: Some("The Second Battle of Adobe Walls was fought on June 27, 1874, when a combined force of Comanche, Kiowa, and Cheyenne warriors attacked a small settlement of buffalo hunters at Adobe Walls in the Texas Panhandle. The hunters, armed with long-range Sharps rifles, held off a much larger force in a fight that marked the opening of the Red River War. The battle demonstrated the devastating effectiveness of the Sharps .45-70 at range against mounted attackers. Among the defenders was the legendary frontiersman Billy Dixon, whose famous shot at 1,538 yards became one of the most celebrated long-range rifle shots in American history."),
    citations: [
        /*[0]*/ "Baker, T. Lindsay — Adobe Walls: A Definitive History",
